  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — Canon\n\n**Headline finding:** there is no test infrastructure in either layer today. `web/package.json` has no test runner or `test` script; `engine/pyproject.toml` lists `pytest` as a dev dependency but there's no `tests/` directory, no `conftest.py`, no pytest config, and zero test files anywhere in the repo. `npx drizzle-kit migrate` also hasn't been run yet (per `HANDOFF.md`), so there's no live schema to run integration tests against either.\n\nMore importantly: **~34 of the ~40 functions in `engine/`** are literal `raise NotImplementedError(\"Phase N — see AGENTS.md ...\")` stubs — this is a scaffolded Phase-1 codebase, not a partially-tested one. That reframes the task: for the stubs, \"coverage gaps\" really means *TDD pinning specs to write before/while implementing each phase*. For the small slice of code that already has real logic, gaps mean *real, present risk*. I've separated the two below.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Functions/classes with real logic today — untested, present risk\n\nThese execute now. Bugs here are live bugs, not future ones.\n\n| Location | Function/Class | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| `engine/agent/graph.py:40` | `should_auto_apply` | The auto-apply gate. Wrong boundary = wrong resolutions silently applied. |\n| `engine/pipeline/detect.py:33` | `severity_for_orphan` | Feeds the auto-apply gate directly. |\n| `engine/pipeline/schema.py:108` | `rule_specificity` | Determines which survivorship rule wins — silently wrong ordering = wrong resolutions. |\n| `engine/pipeline/schema.py:83-105` | `SurvivorshipRule` (`_prefer_source_needs_a_source`) | Only real validation logic in the schema module. |\n| `engine/pipeline/schema.py` | `CanonModel`/`Match`/`Conflict`/`Resolution` | camelCase↔snake_case aliasing + `ge`/`le` constraints — this **is** the tool contract; if it drifts, `web/` and `engine/` silently disagree. |\n| `engine/main.py:31` | `start_run` (FastAPI route) | Only implemented endpoint. |\n| `web/types/rules.ts` | `ruleSpecificity`, `survivorshipRuleSchema` refine | Web-side mirror of the specificity/validator logic above — **must match `rule_specificity` exactly**. |\n| `web/types/{source,conflict,resolution,run,entity}.ts` | All Zod schemas | Every route handler will validate through these; today nothing exercises them. |\n| `web/lib/cn.ts` | `cn` | Trivial but universal — every styled component depends on it. |\n| `web/lib/db/index.ts` | `getDb` | Env-var guard + HMR-safe singleton caching — easy to get subtly wrong. |\n| `web/lib/server/sources.ts` | `listSources`, `countSourcesBySide` | Only Server Component data-access function that exists. |\n\n### Skeletons\n\n**`engine/tests/test_graph.py`**\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom agent.graph import should_auto_apply, AUTO_APPLY_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD, AUTO_APPLY_MAX_SEVERITY\n\nclass TestShouldAutoApply:\n    def test_applies_at_high_confidence_low_severity(self):\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.95, severity=1) is True\n\n    def test_rejects_below_confidence_threshold(self):\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.84, severity=1) is False\n\n    def test_boundary_confidence_is_inclusive(self):\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=AUTO_APPLY_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD, severity=2) is True\n\n    def test_rejects_above_severity_ceiling(self):\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.99, severity=3) is False\n\n    def test_boundary_severity_is_inclusive(self):\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.90, severity=AUTO_APPLY_MAX_SEVERITY) is True\n\n    def test_both_conditions_required_not_either(self):\n        # high confidence alone must not compensate for high severity\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=1.0, severity=4) is False\n        # low severity alone must not compensate for low confidence\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.0, severity=1) is False\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"severity\", [1, 2, 3, 4])\n    def test_severity_is_never_coerced_outside_1_4(self, severity):\n        # documents the expected domain; should reject/typecheck out-of-range in real usage\n        should_auto_apply(confidence=0.9, severity=severity)\n```\n\n**`engine/tests/test_detect.py`**\n```python\nfrom pipeline.detect import severity_for_orphan, classify, detect\n\ndef test_severity_for_orphan_with_children_is_4():\n    assert severity_for_orphan(has_children=True) == 4\n\ndef test_severity_for_orphan_without_children_is_3():\n    assert severity_for_orphan(has_children=False) == 3\n\n# --- classify() is a stub; these pin the documented contract (AGENTS.md § Severity Model) ---\nclass TestClassify:\n    def test_parent_external_id_diff_is_structural_4(self):\n        cls, sev = classify(\"parentExternalId\", \"ACC-1\", \"ACC-2\")\n        assert (cls, sev) == (\"structural\", 4)\n\n    def test_territory_diff_is_attribute_3(self):\n        cls, sev = classify(\"territory\", \"APAC\", \"APAC-SOUTH\")\n        assert (cls, sev) == (\"attribute\", 3)\n\n    def test_role_name_diff_is_attribute_3(self):\n        assert classify(\"roleName\", \"AE\", \"SDR\")[1] == 3\n\n    def test_owner_id_diff_is_attribute_3(self):\n        assert classify(\"ownerId\", \"u1\", \"u2\")[1] == 3\n\n    def test_arbitrary_non_rollup_field_is_attribute_2(self):\n        cls, sev = classify(\"industry\", \"Software\", \"SaaS\")\n        assert (cls, sev) == (\"attribute\", 2)\n\n    def test_values_folding_to_same_form_is_cosmetic_1(self):\n        cls, sev = classify(\"name\", \"Acme Inc.\", \"ACME INC\")\n        assert (cls, sev) == (\"cosmetic\", 1)\n\n    def test_identical_values_are_not_a_conflict(self):\n        # edge case: classify() contract doesn't say what happens when a==b —\n        # detect() presumably never calls classify on equal values; document/assert that\n        ...\n\n# --- detect() is a stub; pins orphan/duplicate/field-diff behavior ---\nclass TestDetect:\n    def test_field_disagreement_produces_one_conflict_per_field(self):\n        ...\n\n    def test_unmatched_entity_on_side_a_only_is_orphan(self):\n        ...\n\n    def test_two_side_a_records_matching_one_side_b_is_duplicate_severity_4(self):\n        ...\n\n    def test_no_disagreement_produces_no_conflicts(self):\n        ...\n\n    def test_null_vs_present_value_is_a_conflict_not_a_crash(self):\n        # edge case: value_a or value_b is None — classify()/detect() must not assume both present\n        ...\n```\n\n**`engine/tests/test_schema.py`**\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError\nfrom pipeline.schema import SurvivorshipRule, rule_specificity, Match, MatchSignals, Resolution\n\nclass TestRuleSpecificity:\n    def test_wildcard_field_and_type_is_least_specific(self):\n        r = SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"escalate\", description=\"\")\n        assert rule_specificity(r) == 0\n\n    def test_specific_field_wildcard_type(self):\n        r = SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"territory\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"escalate\", description=\"\")\n        assert rule_specificity(r) == 2\n\n    def test_wildcard_field_specific_type(self):\n        r = SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"account\", strategy=\"escalate\", description=\"\")\n        assert rule_specificity(r) == 1\n\n    def test_fully_specific_is_highest(self):\n        r = SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"territory\", entity_type=\"account\", strategy=\"escalate\", description=\"\")\n        assert rule_specificity(r) == 3\n\nclass TestSurvivorshipRuleValidation:\n    def test_prefer_source_without_preferred_source_id_raises(self):\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n            SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"prefer_source\", description=\"\")\n\n    def test_prefer_source_with_preferred_source_id_passes(self):\n        SurvivorshipRule(\n            id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"prefer_source\",\n            preferred_source_id=\"src-a\", description=\"\",\n        )\n\n    def test_non_prefer_source_strategy_does_not_require_source_id(self):\n        SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"most_recent\", description=\"\")\n\nclass TestCanonModelWireFormat:\n    def test_field_names_serialize_to_camel_case(self):\n        m = Match(\n            run_id=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\n            entity_a_id=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002\",\n            entity_b_id=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003\",\n            confidence=0.9, method=\"fuzzy\",\n            signals=MatchSignals(exact_key=False, cosine=0.8, fuzzy_ratio=90.0),\n        )\n        payload = m.model_dump(by_alias=True)\n        assert \"runId\" in payload and \"run_id\" not in payload\n        assert \"entityAId\" in payload\n\n    def test_confidence_out_of_range_rejected(self):\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n            Resolution(conflict_id=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\n                        proposed_value=\"x\", rationale=\"x\", confidence=1.5)\n\n    def test_unknown_field_rejected_extra_forbid(self):\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n            Match.model_validate({\n                \"runId\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\n                \"entityAId\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002\",\n                \"entityBId\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003\",\n                \"confidence\": 0.5, \"method\": \"fuzzy\",\n                \"signals\": {\"exactKey\": True, \"cosine\": 1.0, \"fuzzyRatio\": 100.0},\n                \"unexpectedField\": \"should be rejected\",\n            })\n```\n\n**`engine/tests/test_main.py`** (FastAPI, `httpx.AsyncClient` / `TestClient`)\n```python\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom main import app\n\nclient = TestClient(app)\n\ndef test_start_run_accepts_and_echoes_run_id():\n    run_id = \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\"\n    resp = client.post(\"/runs\", json={\"runId\": run_id})\n    assert resp.status_code == 200\n    assert resp.json() == {\"runId\": run_id, \"accepted\": True}\n\ndef test_start_run_rejects_missing_run_id():\n    resp = client.post(\"/runs\", json={})\n    assert resp.status_code == 422\n\ndef test_start_run_rejects_non_uuid_run_id():\n    resp = client.post(\"/runs\", json={\"runId\": \"not-a-uuid\"})\n    assert resp.status_code == 422\n\ndef test_start_run_returns_immediately_without_blocking_on_execute_run(monkeypatch):\n    # error handling gap: execute_run raises NotImplementedError today.\n    # If it runs as a background task, that exception must not surface on\n    # the HTTP response, or every real POST /runs currently 500s silently\n    # in a background thread with no audit_log entry. Worth pinning now.\n    ...\n\ndef test_run_status_currently_returns_501_not_a_silent_wrong_answer():\n    # pins the intentional stub state (AGENTS.md Phase 1) so it fails loudly\n    # when someone accidentally \"half-implements\" it later\n    resp = client.get(\"/runs/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/status\")\n    assert resp.status_code == 501\n```\n\n**`web/lib/db/index.test.ts`** *(needs a test runner — see §5)*\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\ndescribe(\"getDb\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    vi.resetModules();\n    delete process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n    delete (globalThis as any).canonDb;\n    delete (globalThis as any).canonSql;\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws an actionable error when DATABASE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    expect(() => getDb()).toThrow(/DATABASE_URL is not set/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"caches the connection across calls (HMR safety)\", async () => {\n    process.env.DATABASE_URL = \"postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/db\";\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    expect(getDb()).toBe(getDb());\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`web/types/rules.test.ts`**\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { survivorshipRuleSchema, ruleSpecificity } from \"@/types/rules\";\n\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects prefer_source without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\", description: \"\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts prefer_source with preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\",\n      preferredSourceId: \"src-a\", description: \"\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [{ field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" }, 0],\n    [{ field: \"territory\", entityType: \"*\" }, 2],\n    [{ field: \"*\", entityType: \"account\" }, 1],\n    [{ field: \"territory\", entityType: \"account\" }, 3],\n  ])(\"scores %j as %i\", (partial, expected) => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity(partial as any)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Edge cases not covered (beyond what's in the skeletons above)\n\n- **`should_auto_apply`**: exact-boundary values (`0.85`, severity `2`) — inclusive vs. exclusive matters and isn't obvious from the signature alone.\n- **`rule_specificity` / rule selection**: two rules with *equal* specificity — AGENTS.md says \"ties keep author order, first match wins,\" but `rule_specificity` alone can't test that; `select_rule` (still a stub) needs a test asserting list order breaks ties, not sort stability of some other field.\n- **`classify`**: field name present in both `STRUCTURAL_FIELDS` and hypothetically extended lists later — a field that folds to equal *and* is in `OWNERSHIP_FIELDS` (cosmetic should win per the documented precedence, but nothing currently enforces order of the checks).\n- **`CanonicalEntity`/Zod `canonicalEntitySchema`**: `attributes` map with `null` values (explicitly allowed by the type) vs. missing keys — normalize() and detect() need to treat \"attribute absent\" differently from \"attribute explicitly null.\"\n- **`SurvivorshipRule` wildcard `\"*\"` on `field`**: nothing currently tests that `\"*\"` is not treated as a literal field name if an entity happens to have a field called `*`.\n- **`Resolution.confidence` at exactly 0.0 and 1.0** — boundary-inclusive per `Field(ge=0.0, le=1.0)`, worth a boundary test given how load-bearing confidence is everywhere downstream.\n- **`fold_name` (once implemented)**: Unicode, already-folded input (idempotence — `fold_name(fold_name(x)) == fold_name(x)`), a legal suffix that's also a real word (`\"Co\"` the country-code vs. `\"Co.\"` the suffix, `\"AG\"` Germany's suffix vs. a two-letter US state-adjacent abbreviation), multiple suffixes chained (`\"Acme Pvt Ltd Inc.\"`), suffix as a substring not a suffix (`\"Cothing Inc\"`).\n- **`block`/`match` (once implemented)**: empty side A or side B, every record on both sides identical (would exact-key match dominate correctly?), an entity matching >1 candidate above `MIN_MATCH_CONFIDENCE` — which one wins.\n\n---\n\n## 3. New test scenarios suggested (cross-cutting)\n\n1. **Severity-model table-driven test** — one parametrized test asserting the full 1–4 mapping from AGENTS.md's table in one place, so a future edit to `classify`/`severity_for_orphan` that silently breaks the documented model fails immediately, not three call sites later.\n2. **web↔engine contract parity test** (see §5) — golden fixtures round-tripped through both the Zod schema and the Pydantic model.\n3. **Rule evaluation order test** — construct a ruleset with a wildcard rule and a specific rule in *reverse* author order and assert specificity still wins (catches an accidental `sorted()` that's stable on the wrong key).\n4. **Auto-apply threshold sweep smoke test** — once `sweep_auto_apply_threshold` exists, assert monotonicity: escalation rate should not *decrease* as the confidence threshold rises. A violation is a correctness bug in the sweep, not just a metrics curiosity.\n5. **`validate()` non-negotiable check** — table of proposed values that are exactly `value_a`, exactly `value_b`, a \"legal normalization\" of one (whatever that ends up meaning — needs the definition pinned in a test as much as in prose), and a value that's neither → must reject the last case unconditionally, including when it's argued for.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Missing error-handling tests\n\n| Path | Current behavior | Gap |\n|---|---|---|\n| `getDb()` with no `DATABASE_URL` | Throws with actionable message | Untested — regression would silently produce a cryptic Postgres client error instead |\n| Pydantic `extra=\"forbid\"` on every `CanonModel` | Rejects unknown keys | Untested — a typo'd field from `web/` would currently 422 but nothing proves it |\n| `Resolution.confidence` / `Match.confidence` out of `[0,1]` | Rejects via `Field(ge, le)` | Untested |\n| `survivorshipRuleSchema.refine` | Rejects `prefer_source` w/o `preferredSourceId` | Untested (both Zod side and Pydantic side — they must reject the *same* inputs) |\n| `POST /runs` with malformed body | FastAPI 422 | Untested |\n| `GET /runs/:id/status` | Explicit `501` | Untested that it fails loudly rather than defaulting to 200 with empty stats |\n| `execute_run` background task failure | Currently `NotImplementedError`, run inside `BackgroundTasks` | **No test today would catch this exception disappearing silently** — background tasks in FastAPI swallow unhandled exceptions by default; once implemented, a failed run must still reach `status=\"failed\"` + `audit_log` (`run_failed`), not vanish |\n| Connectors' `extract()` (once implemented) | N/A yet | Missing-file (`SyntheticConnector`), auth failure (`SalesforceConnector`), and query error (`WarehouseConnector`) paths all need tests once built — the connector protocol says nothing about how errors propagate |\n| `db.py` writer functions (once implemented) | N/A yet | Need a test asserting attempted writes to `sources`/`rulesets` from the engine are either impossible (no such function exists) or rejected — this is the table-ownership rule from AGENTS.md and today it's enforced by *convention only* |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Integration test gaps (the largest gap, given the two-layer architecture)\n\nThis is where the highest-value tests live once Phase 1–3 land, because the whole design is organized around a boundary that's easy to silently violate.\n\n- **Contract parity test** — the single most valuable integration test to write early: round-trip a fixture through `web/types/*.ts` (Zod `.parse`) and `engine/pipeline/schema.py` (Pydantic `.model_validate`) and assert identical accepted/rejected sets. AGENTS.md says \"do not change one side without changing the other in the same commit\" — nothing currently *checks* that.\n  ```python\n  # engine/tests/test_contract_parity.py\n  # Loads shared JSON fixtures from a fixtures/ dir also readable by a\n  # matching web/types/*.test.ts, so both sides assert against the same data.\n  import json, pytest\n  from pathlib import Path\n  from pipeline.schema import CanonicalEntity, SurvivorshipRule, Conflict, Resolution\n\n  FIXTURES = Path(__file__).parent / \"fixtures\" / \"contract\"\n\n  @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"name,model\", [\n      (\"canonical_entity\", CanonicalEntity),\n      (\"survivorship_rule\", SurvivorshipRule),\n      (\"conflict\", Conflict),\n      (\"resolution\", Resolution),\n  ])\n  def test_valid_fixtures_parse(name, model):\n      for fixture in json.loads((FIXTURES / f\"{name}.valid.json\").read_text()):\n          model.model_validate(fixture)\n\n  @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"name,model\", [\n      (\"survivorship_rule\", SurvivorshipRule),\n  ])\n  def test_invalid_fixtures_are_rejected(name, model):\n      for fixture in json.loads((FIXTURES / f\"{name}.invalid.json\").read_text()):\n          with pytest.raises(Exception):\n              model.model_validate(fixture)\n  ```\n\n- **Table-ownership enforcement** — currently a comment/docstring rule, not a test. Once `db.py` is implemented, add an integration test against a real (or Testcontainers) Postgres where the engine's DB role has no `INSERT`/`UPDATE` grant on `sources`/`rulesets`, and assert `write_entities`/`write_matches`/etc. exist for owned tables only — i.e., there is *no function in `db.py` capable of writing `sources` or `rulesets`* is itself a static/structural assertion worth a test (`assert not hasattr(db, \"write_sources\")`, or a grep-based check in CI).\n\n- **Full run lifecycle E2E** — doesn't exist yet on either side (`web/app/api/runs` isn't built; `execute_run` is a stub). Once both exist:\n  ```python\n  # engine/tests/test_run_lifecycle.py  (needs a test Postgres — testcontainers or a local Supabase)\n  def test_full_run_transitions_queued_to_complete(db_session, seeded_sources_and_ruleset):\n      run_id = create_run_row(db_session, seeded_sources_and_ruleset)\n      execute_run(run_id)\n      row = fetch_run(db_session, run_id)\n      assert row.status == \"complete\"\n      assert row.stats[\"conflicts\"] > 0\n      assert audit_log_has(db_session, run_id, \"run_started\")\n      assert audit_log_has(db_session, run_id, \"conflict_detected\")\n\n  def test_run_that_fails_mid_pipeline_lands_in_failed_not_stuck(db_session, broken_source):\n      run_id = create_run_row(db_session, broken_source)\n      execute_run(run_id)\n      row = fetch_run(db_session, run_id)\n      assert row.status == \"failed\"\n      assert row.error is not None\n      assert audit_log_has(db_session, run_id, \"run_failed\")\n  ```\n\n- **`engine/eval/harness.py` end-to-end** — this is the paper's core deliverable per AGENTS.md and currently has *zero* coverage because every function it calls is a stub:\n  ```python\n  # engine/tests/test_harness_e2e.py\n  def test_seed_42_is_reproducible(tmp_path):\n      m1 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"run_a\")\n      m2 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"run_b\")\n      assert m1 == m2  # same seed → byte-identical manifest\n\n  def test_baseline_rules_beats_baseline_exact_on_precision(tmp_path):\n      manifest = generate(seed=42, accounts=200, out_dir=tmp_path)\n      exact = run_system(\"baseline_exact\", manifest, tmp_path)\n      rules = run_system(\"baseline_rules\", manifest, tmp_path)\n      assert rules.precision >= exact.precision\n\n  def test_canon_full_escalates_the_ambiguous_injection_type(tmp_path):\n      # AGENTS.md: \"deliberately inject cases where the correct answer is\n      # escalate, and score the system on whether it escalates them\"\n      manifest = generate(seed=42, accounts=200, out_dir=tmp_path)\n      ambiguous = [m for m in manifest if m.expected_resolution == \"escalate\"]\n      metrics = run_system(\"canon_full\", manifest, tmp_path)\n      assert metrics.escalation_precision > 0.8  # threshold TBD by the team\n\n  def test_ablation_without_validate_produces_measurable_invented_values(tmp_path):\n      manifest = generate(seed=42, accounts=200, out_dir=tmp_path)\n      metrics = ablate_without_validate(manifest, tmp_path)\n      # this ablation exists specifically to PROVE validate() is non-optional —\n      # the test should fail if removing it produces zero invented values,\n      # because that would undercut the paper's own claim\n      assert metrics.false_auto_apply_rate > run_system(\"canon_full\", manifest, tmp_path).false_auto_apply_rate\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## Recommendation on next step\n\nTwo different actions are gated by AGENTS.md's dependency policy:\n\n1. **`engine/`** — `pytest` is already a declared dependency; I can add `engine/tests/` with the skeletons above (plus a `conftest.py` and `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` block) right now with no new libraries.\n2. **`web/`** — there is 